  {
   "n": 14,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>In this question, the three elements i.e. Mercury, Metal and Zinc have some inter linkage. The inter linkage may fit into one of the following four diagrams. Identify the diagram which most aptly defines this relationship.</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/28/28d7c1f40b24ac1d5e25.png\" />"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/56/5676e6dc1037f1a2953e.png\" />"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9a/9a40d490c8e02ab9b529.png\" />"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/72/726652bda3109dbaa4aa.png\" />"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>(b)<br />\nMercury and Zinc &ndash; both are metals. Thus, the diagram with a larger circle representing &ldquo;Metal&rdquo;<br />\nand two smaller separate circles completely enclosed within it representing Mercury and Zinc<br />\naccurately depicts this relationship.</p>"
  },
  {
   "n": 15,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>In a multiple choice question paper having 30 questions, the marking scheme is as under:<br />\n+5 marks for each correct question;<br />\n+1 mark for each unanswered question;<br />\nNo score for wrong response.<br />\nA group of four students named Arun, Bishal, Chetan and Dhawal gave the following statements:<br />\nArun: My score is 141<br />\nBishal: I have scored 144<br />\nChetan: My score is 147<br />\nDhawal: I scored 139.<br />\nOnly one of the students has got a valid score. What is the name of that student?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "Arun"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Bishal"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Chetan"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "Dhawal"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a)<br />\n&bull; If Chetan has scored 147, it means he has done 29 questions correctly i.e. 29 &times; 5 = 145 but the<br />\n30<sup>th</sup> question can give him 0 or 1 leading to possible score of 145 or 146. Thus, Chetan&rsquo;s score<br />\nis not valid.<br />\n&bull; Bishal has scored 144 implies that he could have done 28 questions correctly leading to a score<br />\nof 28 &times; 5 = 140 but remaining 2 questions can possibly give score of 2 or 1 or 0 depending on<br />\nhis incorrect attempts. This leads to possible scores of 140 or 141 or 142 leading to possibility<br />\nof option &lsquo;a&rsquo; being correct option. Thus, Arun&#39;s score of 141 is vaid [28 questions answered<br />\ncorrectly, 1 unaswered question and 1 wrongly answered].<br />\n&bull; Dhawal having scored 139 means that he has attempted 27 questions correctly leading to a<br />\nscore of 27 &times; 5 = 135 but remaining 3 questions can possibly give maximum score of 3 i.e. total<br />\npossible score = 138. Thus, Dhawal&rsquo;s score is not valid.</p>"
  },
